The outside world was unknown to her, but she could see a glimpse of it through the window in his room.

Hallow and blank, a world one might describe as made of nothingness. An un-space. A place so without form and sense that you could find no way to focus your eyes, and so they'd aimlessly searched the black nothingness, growing ever more tired as they strain and strain. A most unpleasant experience, one she had vowed to avoid it at all costs.

Instead, she focused on the place contained within the walls around them. It seemed so strange when she first arrived here, this room

But now, in this moment? She stared out it, eyes widened in horror. Beyond the blackness flashed a sliver of light. Like a line across the bleak expanse, this flash of light marked something new. It gave her something to focus on. The brightness of it blinded her briefly, and she blinked.

--

Hallow and black. Nothingness.

It wasn’t always that way.

But he’s dying now. Hes been dying.

And with him is dying this place.

This only stable place.

The world around has always fallen apart. For years he would awaken and they would explore this place.

She had always been in this room. At least as long as she could remember. Which wasn’t that long as she had suffered a major head injury when he had rescued her and brought her here. It was through him she remembered everything about this world. He had saved her. He had protected her.

Now she stared out the window in silent horror. He had died and as the hours passed by, the weather seemed to progress. A long stretch of dead and frozen landscape. White covering all surfaces and now the window itself is beginning to crack. In fact, as the time passes since his collapse, the world seems to freeze even more.
((she is in this room. Outside is darkness, occasional flashes of her own fears. No way to calm down. He calmed her down. Now he is dead. ))

Frozen world
Melting

Zombie world
Fully overtaken by zombies
New disease making people human again